{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_design_05_warehouse_shared_warehouse", "label": "\uacf5\uc6a9 \ucc3d\uace0 1\uac1c (A-1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \ud655\uc815\ub41c \uc124\uacc4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_design_05_warehouse_production_halt", "label": "\ucc3d\uace0 \uac00\ub4dd \ucc38 \u2192 \uc0dd\uc0b0 \uc911\ub2e8 (C-a)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \ucc3d\uace0 \ub3d9\uc791 (\uac00\ub4dd \ucc38)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A full warehouse halts every factory until the player harvests, sells, or upgrades. This is the pressure valve that makes warehouse upgrades a real goal rather than an optional convenience."}, {"id": "docs_design_05_warehouse_land_slot", "label": "\ucc3d\uace0\uc758 \ud1a0\uc9c0 \uc2ac\ub86f \uc810\uc720 (D-2)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \ud1a0\uc9c0 \uc2ac\ub86f \ucc28\uc9c0 (D-2)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The warehouse consumes one land slot like a factory, so a default 3x3 land leaves 8 buildable slots. It cannot be demolished because it is a mandatory building. Note the current Prisma schema has no slotX/slotY on Warehouse, so the occupancy is designed but not yet enforced (U-7)."}, {"id": "docs_design_05_warehouse_capacity_formula", "label": "\ucc3d\uace0 \uc6a9\ub7c9 \uacf5\uc2dd 3,000 \u00d7 3^(\ub4f1\uae09\u22121)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \ucc3d\uace0 \ub4f1\uae09 & \uc6a9\ub7c9", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_design_05_warehouse_upgrade_cost_table", "label": "\ucc3d\uace0 \uc5c5\uadf8\ub808\uc774\ub4dc \ube44\uc6a9 \ud14c\uc774\ube14 (\ub4f1\uae09 1~10)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \ucc3d\uace0 \ub4f1\uae09 & \uc6a9\ub7c9", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Capacity scales a uniform x3 per grade, but cost does NOT: money rises exactly x10 every two grades (alternating x3 and x3.33) and the required material escalates wood -> steel -> car. The table in this doc is the truth and WAREHOUSE_UPGRADE_COST in packages/game-core must match it; assuming a flat x3 cost curve is the common mistake."}, {"id": "docs_design_05_warehouse_design_intent", "label": "\ucc3d\uace0 1\ub4f1\uae09 \u2248 16\uc2dc\uac04 \uc124\uacc4 \uc758\ub3c4", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \ucc3d\uace0 \ub4f1\uae09 & \uc6a9\ub7c9 (\uc124\uacc4 \uc758\ub3c4)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Grade 1 (3,000 slots) is sized to roughly 16 hours of one starting factory. As factories multiply the warehouse fills faster, creating natural upgrade pressure \u2014 the mechanism that drives frequent early logins and supplies a growth goal."}, {"id": "docs_design_05_warehouse_volume_coefficient", "label": "\uc790\uc7ac\ubcc4 \ubd80\ud53c \uacc4\uc218 MATERIAL_VOLUME (#21 \uacb0\uc815 4)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \ubd80\ud53c \uacc4\uc218 (#21 \uacb0\uc815 4)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Capacity is counted in units while T1 output is normalized in money (300~400\uc6d0/tick), so high-unit-price low-output factories almost never filled the warehouse and the 16h login-pressure intent broke (mine 33.3h, oil well 62.5h). Per-material coefficients (ORE 2, CRUDE_OIL 5) pull every T1 factory back into the 16h \u00b125% band. Coefficients are integers only because all warehouse math is bigint and fractional factors cannot multiply without precision loss."}, {"id": "docs_design_05_warehouse_t1_only_coefficient", "label": "\ubd80\ud53c \uacc4\uc218\ub97c T1 \uc5d0\ub9cc \uc801\uc6a9\ud558\ub294 \uc774\uc720", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "### \uc65c T1 \uc5d0\ub9cc \uc8fc\ub294\uac00", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scaling coefficients with unit price across all materials would equalize warehouse occupancy per won, erasing 'processing frees storage' \u2014 the very reason T2/T3 exist. Since the tier profit-multiple goal was abandoned (#21 decision 3), volume efficiency became T2/T3's defining value, so coefficients apply to T1 raw materials only."}, {"id": "docs_design_05_warehouse_tier_volume_efficiency", "label": "\ud2f0\uc5b4\ubcc4 \ucc3d\uace0 1\uce78\ub2f9 \uac00\uce58 (T2 4.78\ubc30 \u00b7 T3 42.96\ubc30)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "### \uc65c T1 \uc5d0\ub9cc \uc8fc\ub294\uac00", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_design_05_warehouse_existing_stock_clamp", "label": "\uae30\uc874 \uc7ac\uace0 \ucd08\uacfc \uc2dc computeFree 0 \ud074\ub7a8\ud504", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "### \uae30\uc874 \uc7ac\uace0 \ucc98\ub9ac", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Introducing coefficients can push already-stored inventory past capacity. computeFree clamps a negative remainder to 0, so materials are never destroyed \u2014 only harvesting stops, and the player resolves it by selling or upgrading."}, {"id": "docs_design_05_warehouse_units_vs_volume", "label": "\uac1c\uc218(units) \ub300 \ubd80\ud53c(slots) \ub2e8\uc704 \uad6c\ubd84", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \uc6a9\ub7c9 \uacc4\uc0b0 \uc608\uc2dc", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Capacity, headroom and clamping are all expressed in slots (volume) while production and sale quantities are in units. Mixing the two silently corrupts capacity math, so conversion must go through volumeOf / unitsThatFit."}, {"id": "docs_design_05_warehouse_warehouse_interface", "label": "Warehouse \ub370\uc774\ud130 \uad6c\uc870 (\uc81c\uc548)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \ub370\uc774\ud130 \uad6c\uc870 (\uc81c\uc548)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_design_05_warehouse_warehousestack", "label": "WarehouseStack (warehouseId + material unique, count BigInt)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \uad00\ub828 \uc2a4\ud0a4\ub9c8", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_game_core_src_simulation_targets_checkwarehousebottleneck", "label": "checkWarehouseBottleneck", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \ubd80\ud53c \uacc4\uc218", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_game_core_src_simulation_targets_checkwarehousevaluedensity", "label": "checkWarehouseValueDensity", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \ubd80\ud53c \uacc4\uc218", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_game_core_src_warehouse_capacity_material_volume", "label": "MATERIAL_VOLUME", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \ubd80\ud53c \uacc4\uc218 (#21 \uacb0\uc815 4)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_game_core_src_warehouse_capacity_warehouse_upgrade_cost", "label": "WAREHOUSE_UPGRADE_COST", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \ucc3d\uace0 \ub4f1\uae09 & \uc6a9\ub7c9", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_design_05_warehouse_production_halt", "target": "docs_design_05_warehouse_shared_warehouse", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \ud655\uc815\ub41c \uc124\uacc4", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_design_05_warehouse_capacity_formula", "target": "docs_design_05_warehouse_design_intent", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "## \ucc3d\uace0 \ub4f1\uae09 & \uc6a9\ub7c9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_design_05_warehouse_upgrade_cost_table", "target": "packages_game_core_src_warehouse_capacity_warehouse_upgrade_cost", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "\ucf54\ub4dc \uae30\uc900 packages/game-core WAREHOUSE_UPGRADE_COST", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_design_05_warehouse_volume_coefficient", "target": "packages_game_core_src_warehouse_capacity_material_volume", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "MATERIAL_VOLUME (packages/game-core/src/warehouse/capacity.ts)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_design_05_warehouse_volume_coefficient", "target": "docs_design_05_warehouse_design_intent", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/design/05-warehouse.md", "source_location": "### \uc65c \ud544\uc694\ud588\u